<title>NETHERLANDS: NAGRON H1 NET PROFIT RISES 15 PCT.</title>
<headline>NAGRON H1 NET PROFIT RISES 15 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>First half 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net per shr (guilders)	     5.95 vs   5.37</p>
<p>    Net profit			     9.9  vs   8.6</p>
<p>    Turnover			     178.4  vs 176.2</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    20.57 vs  18.07</p>
<p>    Interest charges		     5.68 vs   5.26</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			15.26 vs  13.23</p>
<p>    Tax					5.34 vs   4.60</p>
<p>NOTES - Nagron said the rise in first-half profits was</p>
<p>largely attributable to the positive development of the Dutch</p>
<p>housing market, noting strong demand for owner-occupied housing.</p>
<p>It said falling prices for non-ferrous metals put pressure</p>
<p>on results of the metal-trading businesses, leading to lower</p>
<p>profits in that sector compared with the first half of 1995.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
